WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.990
- Yeah, I hate to tell you,

00:00:01.990 --> 00:00:02.894
but you are wrong about the Constitution.

00:00:02.894 --> 00:00:04.000
(stamp thumping)

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.060
It's not your fault,

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:07.860
I mean, that thing is
like seven pages long.

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.090
Who has time to read that?

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:12.150
And there's like two
dozen amendments, pff.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:13.560
But it's not your fault,

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:16.130
everyone is wrong about the Constitution.

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:17.077
Think about this phrase,

00:00:17.077 --> 00:00:17.910
(air whooshing)
from each according

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:18.743
to his ability,

00:00:18.743 --> 00:00:20.520
to each according to his needs.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.100
In 1987, the Hearst
Corporation conducted a survey

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.740
to mark the bicentennial
of the US Constitution.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.320
Over 50% of survey participants
thought that that phrase

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.380
from each according to his ability,

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:31.680
to each according to his needs,

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:33.810
was part of the US Constitution.

00:00:33.810 --> 00:00:35.870
And this wasn't a one-off result.

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:38.110
According to a 2002
Columbia Law School study,

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:40.030
nearly two thirds of persons polled,

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:42.110
thought that this phrase
came from the Constitution

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:44.170
or from one of the founding fathers.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.910
But this phrase does not
appear in the Constitution.

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:48.700
James Madison, the author
of the Constitution,

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:49.840
didn't say it either.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:51.140
So who did?

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:52.040
Well, this was written

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:54.750
by none other than Karl Marx in 1875,

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.980
and then parodied by George
Orwell in "Animal Farm".

00:00:57.980 --> 00:01:00.160
Marx wasn't the first person
to articulate this idea.

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.380
Scholars traced the concept
to the New Testament,

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:03.410
which states, in part,

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:05.900
and distribution was made unto every man,

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:08.160
according as he had need.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.280
Now, the Soviet Union eventually
incorporated the slogan

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:12.967
into it's Constitution as, quote,

00:01:12.967 --> 00:01:14.737
"From each according to his ability,

00:01:14.737 --> 00:01:16.920
"to each according to his work."

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:20.680
But that has never appeared
in the US Constitution.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.610
So you can imagine if Americans
confuse the US Constitution

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:25.660
with the Soviet Constitution,

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:28.590
they're probably wrong about
a whole bunch of other things.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:29.620
Let's talk about it.

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:31.730
One thing that people
get wrong all the time

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:33.259
is thinking that the Constitution mandates

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:34.190
(air whooshing)
that English

00:01:34.190 --> 00:01:37.160
is the official language
of the United States.

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:40.310
That same 1987 Hearst
survey found that 64%

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:41.940
of the people believed
that the Constitution

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:45.060
made English the official
national language of America.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.640
But English as the official language

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:48.970
has never been part of the Constitution.

00:01:48.970 --> 00:01:51.040
Although, English was
the dominant language

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:52.950
at the time the Constitution was ratified,

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.850
many other languages flourished as well.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:01:57.490
The most common languages
included Dutch, French, German,

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:00.170
and the many languages
spoken by Native Americans.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:02.000
Enslaved people spoke African languages

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:04.780
as well as made their own
English based Creole languages.

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.610
And most of the founding fathers

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:08.480
favored bilingual education.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:09.851
Thomas Jefferson spoke English,

00:02:09.851 --> 00:02:11.170
(air whooshing)
French, Italian, Latin

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:13.520
and he could also read Greek and Spanish.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.590
He hoped that America
would establish colleges

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:17.710
that would teach in
French, Spanish, German,

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:18.840
and other languages.

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:21.070
Others, like Ben Franklin,
saw it differently,

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:21.903
and said things

00:02:21.903 --> 00:02:22.865
that were incredibly
offensive and Malthusian,

00:02:22.865 --> 00:02:23.970
(air whooshing)

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:26.087
saying, quote, "Those
Germans who come hither

00:02:26.087 --> 00:02:27.347
"are generally the most ignorant,

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:29.177
"stupid sort of their own nation.

00:02:29.177 --> 00:02:30.897
"They will soon outnumber us,

00:02:30.897 --> 00:02:33.487
"that all the advantages we
have will not, in my opinion,

00:02:33.487 --> 00:02:34.957
"be able to preserve our language

00:02:34.957 --> 00:02:38.510
"and even our government
will become precarious."

00:02:38.510 --> 00:02:41.650
Luckily, he didn't win
the day on that one.

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:43.500
Now, states with large German populations

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:45.650
disagreed with Ben Franklin,
at least initially.

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:46.890
In the 1800s,

00:02:46.890 --> 00:02:49.300
Pennsylvania and Ohio
passed laws allowing German

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:51.230
to be taught in public schools.

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:53.910
Of course, however, Americans
have consistently attempted

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:56.790
to limit the speaking of other
languages in this country.

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:57.630
Politicians have tried

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:59.160
to introduce Constitutional amendment

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.240
making English the official language,

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:02.190
which would force the government

00:03:02.190 --> 00:03:04.680
to stop providing bilingual services.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:06.660
So far, these efforts have failed.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:09.150
And while a Constitutional
amendment hasn't passed,

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:11.700
Congress historically has
passed all kinds of laws

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:12.830
that would prevent people

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:15.000
from speaking non-English languages.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:16.190
For example, in the 19th century,

00:03:16.190 --> 00:03:17.840
the government forced
Native American children

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:19.510
to attend missionary schools.

00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:22.170
In 1887, the Bureau of
Indian Affairs decided

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.580
that mission schools on
reservations were required

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.960
to provide all instruction in English.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:29.010
Children who used their
own languages were bullied

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.430
and beaten by the instructors.

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:33.210
This, of course, led to
immense language loss.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:35.870
And, of course, French
was the dominant language

00:03:35.870 --> 00:03:38.840
in the Louisiana territory
for over 100 years.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:40.760
The first Louisiana
Constitutions made English

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:43.790
and French the official
dual languages of the state.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.340
But Louisiana was a melting
pot for different ethnic groups

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:47.730
and eventually their dialects merged

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:50.120
to produce what we call Louisiana French.

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.350
But in 1921,
(air whooshing)

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:53.430
Louisiana adopted a
new state Constitution,

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:55.830
which reversed the policy
of bilingual rights.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.250
The state banned the teaching

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.772
of French in all public schools,

00:03:58.772 --> 00:03:59.750
(air whooshing)
which highlights one

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:02.370
of the differences between
the US Federal Constitution

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:04.620
and individual state constitutions.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:06.750
But of course, these trends
continue to this day.

00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:07.870
Representative Louie Gohmert

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:10.910
introduced the English
Language Unity Act of 2021,

00:04:10.910 --> 00:04:12.376
which would declare English as the,

00:04:12.376 --> 00:04:13.467
(air whooshing)
quote, "Official language

00:04:13.467 --> 00:04:14.300
"of the United States,

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:16.047
"to establish a uniform
English language rule

00:04:16.047 --> 00:04:16.880
"for naturalization,

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:19.627
"and to avoid misconstructions
of the English language texts

00:04:19.627 --> 00:04:21.147
"of the laws of the United States,

00:04:21.147 --> 00:04:22.637
"pursuant to Congress's power

00:04:22.637 --> 00:04:24.837
"to provide for the general
welfare of the United States,

00:04:24.837 --> 00:04:27.177
"and to establish uniform
rule of naturalization

00:04:27.177 --> 00:04:29.920
"under article one, section
eight of the Constitution."

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:32.580
Of course, the reason that
Gohmert wanted to pass this law

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.870
is because it's not in
the Constitution at all.

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:39.550
And Gohmert's bill was referred
to committee where it died.

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:40.600
But putting language aside,

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:41.760
surely that old chestnut,
(air whooshing)

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.770
no taxation without representation,

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:46.430
found it's way into the
Constitution, right?

00:04:46.430 --> 00:04:48.600
Well, the popular history
of the American revolution

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:49.740
goes something like this.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:50.920
The colonists got so fed up

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:52.800
with King George the third's high taxes

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:55.040
that they chucked British
tea into the Boston Harbor,

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:57.880
decided Americans would hence
forth become coffee drinkers,

00:04:57.880 --> 00:04:59.450
and wrote a Constitution ensuring

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:01.510
that no one would ever be taxed again,

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:03.605
without being adequately represented.

00:05:03.605 --> 00:05:04.670
(record scratching)
Well, as a resident

00:05:04.670 --> 00:05:06.000
of the district of Columbia,

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.070
I would have to take issue
with this particular summary

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:09.360
of American history.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:12.290
In the 1700s, the colonists
objected to the Stamp Act

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.300
and other similar laws
that imposed taxes on them,

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:15.510
because they couldn't vote

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:17.370
and didn't have
representation in parliament.

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:19.450
And in response, the English
came up with a theory

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:20.650
of virtual representation,

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:22.680
which meant that since parliament existed,

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.290
every British subject was represented,

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:26.100
regardless of whether they could vote.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:27.440
Of course, the young American colonists

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:30.540
didn't exactly take to this
early version of Zoom meetings.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:32.660
After all the pontificating
about taxes and voting

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:34.310
and the subsequent War of Independence,

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:35.530
perhaps the biggest surprise of all

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:36.691
is that the taxation
without representation

00:05:36.691 --> 00:05:37.524
(air whooshing)

00:05:37.524 --> 00:05:38.357
(coins clinking)
didn't make it

00:05:38.357 --> 00:05:40.070
into the final cut of the Constitution,

00:05:40.070 --> 00:05:41.940
though the colonists
didn't try hard to work it

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:43.520
into the founding documents.

00:05:43.520 --> 00:05:44.990
The Articles of Confederation,

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:46.827
incorporated a we hate taxes stance

00:05:46.827 --> 00:05:48.750
by denying the federal
government the right

00:05:48.750 --> 00:05:50.340
to levy taxes at all.

00:05:50.340 --> 00:05:51.510
This sounded cool on paper,

00:05:51.510 --> 00:05:53.410
but was a really big mess in reality,

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:54.330
because the new government
couldn't pay it's war debts.

00:05:54.330 --> 00:05:56.310
(air whooshing)

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:58.892
It also couldn't raise enough
money for an army or navy.

00:05:58.892 --> 00:05:59.725
(air whooshing)

00:05:59.725 --> 00:06:01.160
The British occupied
forts in the great lakes,

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.930
while also dumping it's
convicts into the colonies.

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.370
And so, for this and many other reasons,

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:07.360
the Americans had to write
a new governing document,

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:08.820
that eventually became the Constitution.

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:10.490
And you had better well believe

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:13.280
that it gave the federal
government the right to levy taxes.

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:15.440
The problem is they forgot to mention

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:17.280
that in order to levy taxes,

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:19.870
everyone needed to be
adequately represented.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:20.990
The state and local authorities

00:06:20.990 --> 00:06:22.450
also got the power to levy taxes,

00:06:22.450 --> 00:06:23.283
but the end result

00:06:23.283 --> 00:06:25.760
is that the Constitution
doesn't guarantee no taxation

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:27.270
without representation.

00:06:27.270 --> 00:06:28.940
But the motto was still a rallying cry

00:06:28.940 --> 00:06:30.380
for the disenfranchised populations,

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:32.080
especially in the nation's capital

00:06:32.080 --> 00:06:33.910
where I live, Washington DC.

00:06:33.910 --> 00:06:35.910
Which is also the only geographical entity

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:37.280
in the contiguous United States,

00:06:37.280 --> 00:06:38.113
whose citizens must pay taxes
(air whooshing)

00:06:38.113 --> 00:06:38.946
(car engine whirring)

00:06:38.946 --> 00:06:40.140
and register for selective service,

00:06:40.140 --> 00:06:42.870
without having political
representation in Congress.

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:44.060
Well, at least political representation

00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:46.020
that can actually do something.

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:49.290
DC residents pay more taxes
than residents in 22 states,

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:52.210
and pay more money per capita
to the federal government

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:54.140
than any actual state.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.850
Now, we are not the only ones.

00:06:55.850 --> 00:06:57.800
Who else pays taxes
without representation?

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:00.910
Well, undocumented immigrants
pay about $7 billion a year

00:07:00.910 --> 00:07:01.743
in taxes.

00:07:01.743 --> 00:07:02.770
Inmates pay taxes,

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:04.790
and so do formerly incarcerated people,

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:07.300
even if their voting rights
have not been restored.

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:09.720
American children work and
pay sales tax and income tax,

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:11.750
but they lack the
representation of a vote.

00:07:11.750 --> 00:07:13.750
And that's just the tip of the iceberg,

00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:17.200
there's a whole bunch of
taxation without representation

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:18.790
in the United States.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:19.840
And that's probably

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:22.800
because the Constitution
doesn't guarantee that right.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:25.360
Americans hate taxes,
but they love shopping,

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:27.350
and a lot of people think
that they have a right

00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:29.440
to enter a particular store,

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:31.800
or at least they have a right
to contract with other people,

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.430
the freedom to contract.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:34.950
This guy believes he has
a Constitutional right

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:37.270
to eat at the Trump
Grill in New York City.

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:38.590
But here, the police officer contends

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:41.234
that a reservation is not
a Constitutional right.

00:07:41.234 --> 00:07:42.067
- It's not a guarantee.

00:07:42.067 --> 00:07:42.930
- They can't revoke my reservation.

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:44.463
- It's not a guarantee.

00:07:44.463 --> 00:07:46.480
It's not a Constitutional right.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:47.840
- The protestor is in fact wrong

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:48.810
about his Constitutional right

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:50.200
to keep his dinner reservation.

00:07:50.200 --> 00:07:51.456
But this is an interesting question,

00:07:51.456 --> 00:07:52.289
(air whooshing)
do people

00:07:52.289 --> 00:07:53.122
have a Constitutional right

00:07:53.122 --> 00:07:55.090
to enter a store or a restaurant?

00:07:55.090 --> 00:07:57.590
The Constitution is often
silent about most things.

00:07:57.590 --> 00:07:58.710
So it shouldn't be surprising

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:00.280
that no one has an explicit reference

00:08:00.280 --> 00:08:02.210
to where people are allowed to be.

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:03.043
But the 1980 US Supreme Court case

00:08:03.043 --> 00:08:04.490
(air whooshing)

00:08:04.490 --> 00:08:06.490
Pruneyard Shopping Center versus Robins,

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:07.510
said that the Constitution

00:08:07.510 --> 00:08:09.300
does not give people an absolute right

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.560
to enter and remain on private property,

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:13.970
even if they intend to exercise
their first amendment right

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:15.620
to free expression.

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:18.470
So if this man wants to get
into a restaurant to protest,

00:08:18.470 --> 00:08:20.900
he doesn't actually have a
Constitutional right to do so,

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:22.470
despite the first amendment.

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:24.560
But what about if the
city or state government

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:26.730
has imposed a vaccination
requirement to enter?

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.640
Does that violate the Constitution?

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:29.670
Well so far, the answer is no,

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:32.460
because not all unequal
treatment violates federal

00:08:32.460 --> 00:08:33.820
or state laws.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:35.460
The Civil Rights Act of 1964

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:36.760
explicitly prohibits restaurants

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:37.593
from refusing service to
customers based on race,

00:08:37.593 --> 00:08:39.200
(air whooshing)

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.690
color, religion or national origin.

00:08:41.690 --> 00:08:43.880
A restaurant can't refuse
service to black people

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:46.490
or white people or Muslims
or atheists, for example.

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:48.660
But when it comes to
other classes of people,

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:50.910
it's a complete tossup,
they can do what they want.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:52.950
Restaurants and business
owners have argued

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:54.330
that they have a religious right

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:56.710
to refuse service to gay
and transgender people,

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:58.590
because of the owner's religious beliefs.

00:08:58.590 --> 00:08:59.630
Now, the Supreme Court has yet

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:01.210
to definitively settle that issue

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:03.870
and it's going to be very
interesting to see what happens

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:05.890
with the Supreme Court
over the next few years

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:06.900
on this particular issue,

00:09:06.900 --> 00:09:08.630
it's definitely going to come up.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:11.410
But when a local regulation
prevents unvaccinated people

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:12.700
from entering a restaurant,

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:15.640
which is what happened with
the situation in New York City,

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:17.240
we're not talking about a protected

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:19.920
or quasi protected class of
people based on their race,

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:21.300
ethnicity, or gender,

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:23.066
that means a lower standard of review,

00:09:23.066 --> 00:09:24.390
(air whooshing)
in other words,

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:25.570
rational basis review,

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:28.520
which basically no law ever fails.

00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:29.990
So the bottom line is
that the Constitution

00:09:29.990 --> 00:09:31.970
is not going to protect
your dinner reservation

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:34.350
if there is a specific enforceable law

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:36.700
that says you can't go inside.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:37.533
Then there is a phrase

00:09:37.533 --> 00:09:39.365
that I think everyone is familiar with,

00:09:39.365 --> 00:09:40.198
(air whooshing)
the idea

00:09:40.198 --> 00:09:41.760
that the criminal law presumes

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.270
that you are innocent until proven guilty.

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.150
Now, that idea that you
are presumed innocent

00:09:46.150 --> 00:09:46.983
until proven guilty,

00:09:46.983 --> 00:09:49.830
is one of the most significant
principles in American law.

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:51.300
The rights of criminal defendants

00:09:51.300 --> 00:09:53.040
are very much part of the Constitution.

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:53.873
For example,
(paper rustling)

00:09:53.873 --> 00:09:55.090
the Fifth Amendment
bars self-incrimination,

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:57.527
quote, "No person shall be
compelled in any criminal case

00:09:57.527 --> 00:09:58.991
"to be a witness against himself."

00:09:58.991 --> 00:09:59.824
(air whooshing)
This is known

00:09:59.824 --> 00:10:01.230
as the right to remain silent.

00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:02.150
The Sixth Amendment requires
(paper rustling)

00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:04.610
that people be given a speedy
and impartial jury trial,

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:06.530
an attorney in criminal prosecutions

00:10:06.530 --> 00:10:08.110
and establishes defendant's right

00:10:08.110 --> 00:10:10.100
to confront adverse witnesses.
(air whooshing)

00:10:10.100 --> 00:10:11.090
And the 14th Amendment
(paper rustling)

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:13.130
provides for due process of law.

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:14.970
However, the Constitution does not require

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:16.730
that a state prove that
someone committed a crime

00:10:16.730 --> 00:10:17.850
beyond a reasonable doubt,

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:19.320
and the Constitution doesn't say

00:10:19.320 --> 00:10:21.220
that you're innocent until proven guilty.

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:23.070
Now, I'm not saying that
the concept of innocent

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:25.370
until proven guilty is not important.

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:27.640
But the bigger point is that
not all fundamental rights

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.820
can be sourced directly to a line of text

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:31.320
in the Constitution.

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:32.760
Astute Legal Eagles probably already know

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:34.660
that many of our important
legal principles come

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:36.080
from English common law.

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:37.220
But the presumption of innocence

00:10:37.220 --> 00:10:39.330
has a more complicated origin story.

00:10:39.330 --> 00:10:40.810
It isn't found in any of the sources

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:42.610
we traditionally cite
for English common law,

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:46.470
like the Magna Carta, or the
English Bill of Rights of 1689,

00:10:46.470 --> 00:10:49.110
or treatises by Coke and Blackstone.

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:50.390
In fact, this presumption comes

00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:52.270
from Roman law and canon law,

00:10:52.270 --> 00:10:54.340
which formed the common law of Europe.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:56.380
And eventually, this principle
made it's way into common law

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:57.905
in a very roundabout way.

00:10:57.905 --> 00:10:58.750
(air whooshing)
In Coffin

00:10:58.750 --> 00:10:59.620
versus the United States,

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:01.550
the Supreme Court held that
the presumption of innocence

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:02.780
was a bedrock concept

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:04.590
in the American criminal justice system.

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:06.030
Then Justice White credited this

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:07.041
to an Irish jurist named Leonard McNally.

00:11:07.041 --> 00:11:08.670
(air whooshing)

00:11:08.670 --> 00:11:10.570
McNally was known as a zealous advocate

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:12.850
for Irish defendants who
were accused of treason.

00:11:12.850 --> 00:11:14.710
And during McNally's lifetime,

00:11:14.710 --> 00:11:16.220
the British system required two witnesses

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:17.780
to prove someone guilty of treason,

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:19.400
unless the accused was Irish,

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:22.330
in which case one witness was sufficient.

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:24.520
After McNally's death, the
English press found out

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:26.020
that despite his years of advocacy

00:11:26.020 --> 00:11:28.100
for the presumption of Irish innocence,

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:30.590
McNally was, in fact, a double agent.

00:11:30.590 --> 00:11:32.850
He represented Irish
revolutionaries in court,

00:11:32.850 --> 00:11:34.320
but reported on their activities

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:36.780
to prosecutors for at least 26 years.

00:11:36.780 --> 00:11:38.330
Despite McNally's dubious role

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:39.740
as a double agent for the government,

00:11:39.740 --> 00:11:41.860
today the principle of
innocent until proven guilty

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:44.290
is fundamental to the
criminal justice system

00:11:44.290 --> 00:11:45.610
in the United States,

00:11:45.610 --> 00:11:48.240
despite it having no reference whatsoever

00:11:48.240 --> 00:11:49.900
in the Constitution itself.

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:51.440
Now, that's just the tip
of the iceberg of things

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:52.970
that you're wrong about the Constitution.

